// The art in the galleries' insides (js/art.js): a line a work, by site. Fetched with a gallery's inside, never in the first download.
//
// A painting hangs on a wall its inside's JSON lists (`hangs`: tools/models/art_gallery.py in the models' repo), a work a line:
//   { id, wall: '<room>/<wall>', at: m along the wall from its start (the work's middle), y: its middle's height (the model's frame),
//     w, h: its size in m, without the frame, kind, seed, frame, title, artist, year }
//   kind: 'landscape', 'portrait', 'still-life', 'abstract' or 'ink' (a hanging scroll): made up in the browser from `seed`
//     (js/art-paint.js), nothing to download
//   frame: 'gilt', 'timber', 'black', 'white', 'none' (the canvas's edge) or 'scroll' (a silk mount and its roller)
//   ...or a real one: `image: 'art/<file>.jpg'` (in public/art/) in place of kind and seed, the rest as above
// A sculpture stands on a plinth the JSON lists (`plinths`):
//   { id, plinth: '<room>/p<n>', kind: 'bronze', 'marble', 'steel' (painted) or 'vessel', h: its height in m, seed, title, artist, year }
// Each work's label is painted beside it from its title, artist and year.
// To put a real work in place of a made-up one, change its line (ai/misc/adding_art.md in the models' repo): its `id` and wall stay.

